{"id":"57389b11bb1e9431","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-df-incompleteness.md","title":"Gödel–Rosser First Incompleteness Theorem","display":"df-incompleteness — Gödel–Rosser First Incompleteness Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-incompleteness","aliases":["58-df-incompleteness","Gödel Incompleteness"],"display":"df-incompleteness — Gödel–Rosser First Incompleteness Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch07/58-lem-gg.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-consistency.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-zfc-model6-sentence-set.md]]","[[../batch08/58-df-provable.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-incompleteness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-incompleteness</span><span>Gödel Incompleteness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-incompleteness — Gödel–Rosser First Incompleteness Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"967fd715c999aad8\" href=\"?note=967fd715c999aad8\" title=\"../batch07/58-lem-gg.md\">../batch07/58-lem-gg.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6996aaff4caeacce\" href=\"?note=6996aaff4caeacce\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-consistency.md\">../batch13/58-df-consistency.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"b00c32fa4e76ff85\" href=\"?note=b00c32fa4e76ff85\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-zfc-model6-sentence-set.md\">../batch18/58-df-zfc-model6-sentence-set.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"582b96e73e5d1c6e\" href=\"?note=582b96e73e5d1c6e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-provable.md\">../batch08/58-df-provable.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,\\Sigma,Q_\\Sigma,g,S_0\\in V\">\\(T,\\Sigma,Q_\\Sigma,g,S_0\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Q_\\Sigma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(Q_\\Sigma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span> is the fixed Robinson-arithmetic axiom set.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EffectiveTheory}_S(T,\\Sigma,g)\">\\(\\mathrm{EffectiveTheory}_S(T,\\Sigma,g)\\)</span> is the effective-theory predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"967fd715c999aad8\" href=\"?note=967fd715c999aad8\" title=\"../batch07/58-lem-gg.md\">../batch07/58-lem-gg.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)\">\\(\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)\\)</span> is syntactic consistency and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S(\\Sigma,S_0)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S(\\Sigma,S_0)\\)</span> identifies the sentence set.</li>\n<li>Provability uses the fixed proof system of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"582b96e73e5d1c6e\" href=\"?note=582b96e73e5d1c6e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-provable.md\">../batch08/58-df-provable.md</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}incompleteness\\text{-}first}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{EffectiveTheory}_S(T,\\Sigma,g)\n\\land Q_\\Sigma\\subseteq T\n\\land\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S(\\Sigma,S_0)\\\\\n\\to{}&amp;\n\\exists\\varphi\\in S_0\\;\n\\bigl(T\\nvdash\\varphi\\land T\\nvdash\\neg\\varphi\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}incompleteness\\text{-}first}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{EffectiveTheory}_S(T,\\Sigma,g)\n\\land Q_\\Sigma\\subseteq T\n\\land\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S(\\Sigma,S_0)\\\\\n\\to{}&amp;\n\\exists\\varphi\\in S_0\\;\n\\bigl(T\\nvdash\\varphi\\land T\\nvdash\\neg\\varphi\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the Rosser strengthening: ordinary syntactic consistency suffices; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\">\\(\\omega\\)</span>-consistency is not assumed.</li>\n<li>The earlier second-incompleteness line incorrectly placed the meta-level truth value <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)\">\\(\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)\\)</span> where an object-language arithmetic sentence was required. A faithful second theorem needs an explicit consistency sentence, a Gödel coding, a representability theorem for the proof predicate, and derivability conditions; those ingredients are not currently supplied by one reusable upstream atom.</li>\n<li>Consequently this file states exactly the first incompleteness theorem and does not retain the ill-typed second assertion.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Gödel, On Formally Undecidable Propositions</li>\n<li>Mendelson, Introduction to Mathematical Logic</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch07/58-lem-gg.md","status":"resolved","id":"967fd715c999aad8","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-lem-gg.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-consistency.md","status":"resolved","id":"6996aaff4caeacce","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-consistency.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-zfc-model6-sentence-set.md","status":"resolved","id":"b00c32fa4e76ff85","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-zfc-model6-sentence-set.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-provable.md","status":"resolved","id":"582b96e73e5d1c6e","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-provable.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-lem-gg.md","status":"resolved","id":"967fd715c999aad8","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{EffectiveTheory}_S(T,\\Sigma,g)$ is the effective-theory predicate from [[../batch07/58-lem-gg.md]].","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-provable.md","status":"resolved","id":"582b96e73e5d1c6e","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"Provability uses the fixed proof system of [[../batch08/58-df-provable.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T,\\Sigma,Q_\\Sigma,g,S_0\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"Q_\\Sigma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EffectiveTheory}_S(T,\\Sigma,g)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S(\\Sigma,S_0)","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}incompleteness\\text{-}first}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{EffectiveTheory}_S(T,\\Sigma,g)\n\\land Q_\\Sigma\\subseteq T\n\\land\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S(\\Sigma,S_0)\\\\\n\\to{}&\n\\exists\\varphi\\in S_0\\;\n\\bigl(T\\nvdash\\varphi\\land T\\nvdash\\neg\\varphi\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Con}_S(T)","display":false}],"bytes":2030,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-662","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-incompleteness.md|58-df-incompleteness]]（batch10）"}],"outgoing":["967fd715c999aad8","6996aaff4caeacce","b00c32fa4e76ff85","582b96e73e5d1c6e"]}